  "title": "Roanoke Colony: 115 Settlers Vanished and Left One Word",
  "description": "The Roanoke Colony vanished from an island in North Carolina and left only one word carved into a post: CROATOAN. So where did the Lost Colony go?\n\nIn 1587 about 115 English settlers landed on Roanoke Island. Their governor, John White, sailed back to England for supplies, but the war with Spain and the Spanish Armada kept him away until 1590. When he returned, the houses were taken down, there were no bodies, and the word CROATOAN was carved at the fort's entrance. White had told the colonists to carve a cross if they left in danger. There was no cross.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a strange true story every day. Where do you think the colonists went? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #roanokecolony #lostcolony #unsolvedmysteries #stickstory",
